{"title":"2023 IOQM/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IOQM/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let X be the set of all even positive integers n such that the measure of the angle of some regular polygon is n\ndegrees. Find the number of elements in X.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IOQM/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the regular polygon have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> sides. Since the required angle is even, write it as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56c93c7c1d05c3e495bca79f46ff0e429c991a2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{(s-2)180}{s}=2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"131\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/2/7624230d9681c2c21e2e7b2548bb20c2996f2b5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180s-360=2ns$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"140\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/6/15625e07d9b54f71e3e5dac06cf76cf5a9166402.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2s(90-n)=360$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1bb7595c9a0fba7430bbb387c3206de22c85a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(90-n)=180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/c/f4c3d6a5ac5d60ef15af24beb873bb613678298d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\geq3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/e/24e477a9a26c287ce974b584bc6f6fb525633123.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90-n=\\frac{180}{s}\\leq60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"151\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/2/4a297af4f912c3dae5cbd6d3f8963af3654e8fcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90-n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> must be a positive divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb1b41850ab676e4d1cf15c69b1609af4befbc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>The positive divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb1b41850ab676e4d1cf15c69b1609af4befbc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> not exceeding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/a/c5a6c029bbd2fbfa7cb0af3bbc0ad6981a9e30dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,3,4,5,6,9,10,12,15,18,20,30,36,45,60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"350\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> such divisors, and each gives a distinct positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/4/8f4df434e9309f4ec0187cf62fb5d7ed42bc0f0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=90-d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/2/122be32b3f050309c88e59fbbfdda0fd5e32a498.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nNote: This solution was not made by me (biggest_glitter_hater). It was added by a user (who did not name themselves) on the page containing all problems from the IOQM 2023. I merely shifted the solution here as it was spoiling the problem for those who looked through the page.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018065145\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.015 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.022 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 53/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2857/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:28751:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018065145 and revision id 290666. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}